# Squash-merge pull requests

This repo squash-merges. The PR title becomes the only commit on `main`, so it must be a valid Commitizen subject — the same as the branch's main/primary commit.

```
# ❌ BAD
Add Cursor rules for FastAPI, Python quality, and Commitizen
Update stuff
PR to add notes endpoint

# ✅ GOOD
chore(cursor): add python fastapi and commitizen rules
feat(notes): add create-note request schema
```

## Title rules

- Use `<type>(<scope>): <subject>` from the Commitizen rule. Copy the main commit subject when the branch has one primary commit.
- If the branch has several commits, write one squash title that describes the whole change (still Commitizen). Do not join every commit with commas.
- Do not use sentence case, "Add X", or a summary that drops the type/scope.
- Keep the PR body for Summary / Test plan. Do not put the conventional subject only in the body.

When creating a PR, pass this title to `gh pr create --title`. When the existing PR title does not match, update it.
